;==============================================================================
; console_bankpatch.s - originally generated by
; docs/superpowers/reloc-tools/gen_console_bankpatch.py.
;
; THE GENERATOR CANNOT BE RE-RUN, and saying so beats a header that sends the
; next reader to a tool that aborts.  It is a ONE-SHOT LABELLER: it finds
; unlabelled long load/store sites, names them _kcbNNN/_kcmNNN in the source,
; and emits this table.  Every site is labelled now, so it stops with "some
; sites are labeled / need manual handling" and writes nothing.  Its PATHS map
; was also stale -- it still pointed at src/drivers/console/ after the console
; moved to the far bank -- which is corrected but does not make it runnable.
;
; SO THIS TABLE IS MAINTAINED BY HAND.  Removing a patch site means deleting
; its DA lines here and decrementing the two EQUs at the foot.  Merlin catches
; a DA naming a label that no longer exists; it CANNOT catch a site that lost
; its entry, which shows up as a bank byte left at $02 -- historically a blue
; screen or blank glyphs.  The check that a change here is right is the BOOT:
; smoke reads `ls /' off the rendered console.
;
; Last hand-edit: 2026-10-12, adding _kcm023 for _Con_CopyRingRow.
;
; Self-mod patch table for the console $03 -> _kConsoleBank relocation.  Each DA
; entry is the in-kernel-bank offset of a baked-$03 operand BANK byte that Con_Init
; overwrites with _kConsoleBank.  L-sites (STAL/LDAL CON_*BUF): operand+3.
; M-sites (MVN $03,$03): operand+1 (dst bank) and +2 (src bank).
;==============================================================================
